{% comment %}
  TRMNL "Half Vertical" layout (400x480). A mobile-style column stack: the
  route's two directions stacked top/bottom, each shows a stop chain over the
  matching time chain. Up to 2 trips render per direction, but only the first
  is shown on screen--md and below (`hidden lg:block` on the rest) — TRMNL X's
  extra vertical room is the only size with headroom for a second trip without
  the stack overflowing 480px.

  This intentionally does NOT use the Overflow engine (`data-overflow`,
  see full.liquid and reference/modulations.md in the trmnl-framework
  skill): tested directly, two independent `data-overflow` containers
  stacked in normal document flow (as opposed to side-by-side inside a
  single `.columns`, which is what full.liquid uses and where it works
  correctly) corrupt each other's layout — the second section's content
  renders shifted left and clipped, reproducible with a >4s render wait,
  so it isn't a screenshot-timing artifact. Revisit if a future framework
  version fixes multi-container Overflow outside `.columns`. See
  README.md.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="layout">
  {% if sections.size > 0 %}
  <div class="flex flex--col gap--large w--full">
    {% for sec in sections limit: 2 %}
      <div class="flex flex--col gap--small w--full">
        <span class="title">{{ sec.title }}</span>

        {% if sec.trips.size > 0 %}
          {% for trip in sec.trips limit: 2 %}
            <div class="item{% unless forloop.first %} hidden lg:block{% endunless %}">
              <div class="content">
                <span class="label label--small">{% for stop in trip.stops %}{% unless forloop.first %} &rarr; {% endunless %}{{ stop.name }}{% endfor %}</span>
                <span class="value value--tnums" data-value-fit="true">{% for stop in trip.stops %}{% unless forloop.first %} &rarr; {% endunless %}{{ stop.time }}{% endfor %}</span>
                <span class="label label--small">{{ trip.vehicle }}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
        {% else %}
          <span class="label">No upcoming sailings</span>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% else %}
    <span class="label">{{ error | default: "Set the plugin's agency and route." }}</span>
    {% if detail %}<span class="label label--small">{{ detail }}</span>{% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</div>

<div class="title_bar">
  <img class="image image--adaptive" src="https://usetrmnl.com/images/plugins/private_plugin.svg" />
  <span class="title">{{ route_name | default: "Ferry" }}</span>
  <span class="instance">Updated {{ updated_at }}</span>
</div>
